{
    "name": "WES tertiary analysis from FASTQ (v1)",
    "a_galaxy_workflow": "true",
    "format-version": "0.1",
    "annotation": "Germline whole exome sequencing (WES) analysis from paired-end FASTQ to a prioritised, annotated variant table.\n\nRuns once per sample of a list:paired collection (element identifiers are used as sample names):\n\n1. Read QC (FastQC) and adapter/quality trimming (fastp).\n2. Alignment to the reference with BWA-MEM (read groups set from the sample name), duplicate marking\n   (Picard MarkDuplicates) and alignment statistics (samtools stats).\n3. Exome capture QC: Picard CollectHsMetrics (on-target rate, fold-80, % target bases >= 20x) and per-target\n   coverage with mosdepth (bases at 1/10/20/30/50x per target, for gap analysis).\n4. Germline variant calling with FreeBayes (standard input filters: MAPQ >= 30, BQ >= 20).\n5. Tertiary analysis, the embedded \"WES tertiary analysis from VCF (v2)\" workflow: normalisation, restriction\n   to the padded targets, quality filtering, ClinVar + gnomAD + SnpEff annotation, prioritisation and tables.\n6. One MultiQC report for all samples (FastQC, fastp, Picard, samtools, bcftools stats, SnpEff).\n\nReference FASTA, target BED, ClinVar and gnomAD must use the same genome build and chromosome naming.\n",
    "tags": [
        "WES",
        "exome",
        "germline",
        "variant-calling",
        "variant-annotation",
        "variant-prioritization",
        "tertiary-analysis"
    ],
    "license": "MIT",
    "release": "0.1",
    "uuid": "e4cd5a16-74be-5629-a676-4542c043ea15",
    "comments": [],
